      "id": "eye7o",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{R}{\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{R}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/fgD1Exzuy93lV8IMDTH8m3XsIeZaAx747bo-QqtXg9Y.original.fullsize.png\">\r\n$x^{2}+y^{2}=R^{2}$\r\n$2 x+2 y \\frac{d y}{d x}=0$\r\n$\\frac{d y}{d x}=-\\frac{x}{y}=\\tan 45^{\\circ}=1$\r\n$\\therefore x=-\\frac{R}{\\sqrt{2}}$\r\n$y=+\\frac{R}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
